==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Uniform Motion|25}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Coffin Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
*8 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*5 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*2 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 100~103.33 seconds<sup>3,000f~3,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns after 85.33 seconds<sup>2,560f</sup>.
*1 [[Deathshund]] spawns after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A nasty stage consisting of hard pushing Angelic Gories, the wall of an enemy that is 150% Deathshund, and not one, but 2 awful backliners, this can seem like a painful stage at first glance. Thankfully, Deathshund and Spacefish Jones spawn very late, meaning another strategy can be employed.

Kill the 1st Celeboodle and Gabriel (preferably with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] for extra money), then lure Jones and Zang Roo to the base. Once Zang Roo burrows to the base, try to kill him ASAP with your best Zombie nukers such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], or any high DPS attacker + the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]]. Then use your highest damage nukers like Can Can Cat, Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], in addition to [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] to rush burst down Sunfish Jones.

